.TH MV 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
mv \- move (rename) files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mv
[\fB\-i\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR] \fISOURCE\fR... \fIDEST\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rename SOURCE to DEST, or move SOURCE(s) into an existing directory DEST. Falls back to a copy-then-delete when the rename crosses a filesystem boundary, preserving modification time in that fallback.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-interactive
Prompt before overwriting an existing destination.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR (print a usage line and exit) and \fB\-\-version\fR. Commands that take file/path arguments also accept \fB\-\-\fR to mark the end of options, so a file literally named e.g. \fB\-oddfile\fR can still be referenced.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on a general failure (a listed file could not be processed, etc.), 2 on a usage error (missing or invalid arguments).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mitos\-box (1),
.BR mitos\-utils\-compat (7),
.BR mitos\-utils\-integration (7)
